verything (good cooperation). Weakness: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Egocentric may affect crew cooperation, but \"puts concern for others above everything\" suggests good teamwork. Communication difficulty could be mitigated? Not sure.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Weakness: pretentious, sometimes wrong tone, makes nasty remarks about colleagues (crew cooperation issue). Also weak memory for numbers (attention/accuracy). So cooperation concerns.\n\nCandidate C: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership. Weakness: unfriendly, eats unhealthily (maybe irrelevant), regarded as show-off, not open to new ideas (cooperation, adaptability). So cooperation concerns.\n\nCandidate D: responds adequately to unexpected events, concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously. Weakness: moody, loner (possible hot-tempered, know-it-all). Cooperation concerns.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate best overall. Let's weigh.\n\nA: strong decision speed, calm, attention, concern for others (good). Communication difficulty and egocentric may be mitigated; not willing to further education could affect adaptability. But overall maybe strong.\n\nD: strong problem solving, responsibility, concentration, but moody and loner may affect crew. No explicit evidence about stress resilience beyond \"responds adequately to unexpected events\". Not as strong as B's stress handling.\n\nB: strong reliability, stress handling, weather assessment, but nasty remarks and pretentiousness severe.\n\nC: strong situational awareness, leadership, but unfriendly, show-off, not open.\n\nThus A might be best overall: technical competence, calm, quick decisions, attention, concern for others (crew cooperation). Communication difficulty is a concern but maybe less severe than moody/hot temper? Egocentric also concerning. But \"puts concern for others above everything\" suggests teamwork orientation.\n\nWe need to decide. The panel currently has D as leading per Agent 2. Agent 3 can either agree or propose alternative. Let's propose Candidate A as a stronger overall fit, citing evidence: quick correct decisions, calm under pressure, excellent attention, puts concern for others above everything (crew cooperation). Counterpoint: difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric, but we can argue that his concern for others mitigates cooperation concerns, and his decision speed and calmness are critical for long-distance flights. Also note that his unwillingness to further education is a concern but may be less immediate.\n\nThus we can change vote to Candidate A, explaining why we think A outweighs D.\n\nWe must reference Agent 2's point. Provide evidence.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate A\"."}
